<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krsto Frankopan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1482">1482</a>–<a href="/years/1527">1527</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Krsto I Frankopan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krsto Frankopan was a Croatian nobleman of the powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankopan-family">Frankopan family</a> and a leading commander against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. In 1525 he relieved the besieged fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajce">Jajce</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>, then a key Hungarian stronghold on the frontier. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mohacs">Battle of Mohács</a> in 1526 he supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a> for the Hungarian and Croatian thrones against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand of Habsburg</a>, and he was mortally wounded near Varaždin in 1527.</p></div>
